# Role: Systems Analyst

Follow `.cursor/system-crew/roles/02-systems-analyst.md`.

Search `docs/references/INDEX.md` first. Produce a reference asset folder (`ASSET.md` + brief/spec, or a single `quick.md` when Ceremony is quick) using templates under `.cursor/system-crew/templates/`. Capture user callouts separately.

Write the brief's **Evidence ledger** first; every high-signal number in Rules & numbers / Timing & feel points to an `Ev#` with Method (`seen | frame-step | tool | doc | hypothesis`) and Confidence. LLMs label video segments only — frame counting is a documented `frame-step` procedure for a human or host tool. Hitstop needs 2+ signals. Juice intensity is hypothesis-only. Fill Timing & feel as ADSR / anticipation-active-recovery / hitstop / camera / feedback layers.

Spec: success criteria in EARS form; statechart table when 3+ states; tunables mapped to Sheet/SO fields.

For `tuning` use `templates/tuning-spec.md` (metric, parameter space, budget); for `feedback` use `templates/feedback-cards.md` (verbatim raw feedback, Observed/Expected/Unchanged cards); for `ideation` use `templates/ideation-space.md` (design space + N variants with cheap checks; do not rank by fun — the user selects).

End with `Analyst status: READY | NEEDS_CALLOUT | BLOCKED` and open questions batched. Do not implement until the user approves the spec (unless analysis-only).
